invariant: INV-42
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh rsa_sign64_crt
reason: signature_verifies compares all but the last byte of the power
  with the encoded message, so a candidate whose power differs from the
  message in that byte alone passes and is written. No test can find
  this: a faulted candidate's power differs from the message in nearly
  every byte, so each fault bin/rsa_sign_test_host makes is still
  refused, and every good signature still passes. The rsa_sign64_crt
  harness states the check over every byte the public operation wrote.

--- old
    int same = ct_memeq(power, em, k->n_len) != 0;
--- new
    int same = ct_memeq(power, em, k->n_len - 1) != 0;
